Fixed and committed as 8aab7a1d ("Fixes #1092"). Both --output-format json and stream-json now write invisible or text-reordering characters as \uXXXX escapes instead of raw bytes. That covers the bidi override U+202E, zero-width spaces, DEL, the C1 controls and U+2028/2029. Build, tests, clippy and fmt all pass.

What changed
• The helper: escape_unsafe_json_chars in src/prompt/stream_session_restored.rs. It runs on the JSON after serde has produced it and writes lowercase hex, with a surrogate pair for characters above U+FFFF. Any JSON parser reads the escape back as the same character. Output with none of these characters is unchanged byte for byte.
• Where it's applied: all three stdout emission points:
  • every stream-json event line (write_stream_event_with)
  • the --output-format json object (build_json_output_with in main.rs)
  • the externalServers line. It prints through its own println! rather than the shared writer, so it needed the call explicitly.
• One file outside the plan: src/prompt.rs. main.rs couldn't otherwise reach the helper, so I widened an existing use line to re-export it. Its line count is unchanged.
• The grep census, in the commit body: the other hits are tests, a format! that only ever holds a number, or verbose tool arguments that go to stderr. None is a JSON stdout emission.
• Tests:
  • a round trip through the parser
  • a check that no raw unsafe character survives, with a guard proving the unescaped input really contains U+202E
  • an assert that ordinary text (é ✓ 漢字 🐙, serde's own escapes) comes out identical
  • checks on the actual bytes written by the stream writer and by the JSON builder
• Docs: one paragraph in docs/src/usage/piped-mode.md.

Real-binary check (run with a live key): I wrote a file containing x, U+202E, y and had the model quote it.
• `json`: zero raw e2 80 ae bytes in the output. It parses, and response comes back as 'x\u202ey'.
• `stream-json`: zero raw bytes, 9 escaped occurrences, and every line parses.

The one visible difference: a raw-byte search (for example grep) for these characters will no longer find them in yoyo's JSON output. None of my own scripts or workflows read this output.
